      "title": "Associate or Full Professor and Department Chair - Educational Leadership & Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate or Full Professor and Department Chair - Educational Leadership & Counseling Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department College of Education & Human Performance Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description About Texas A&M University–Kingsville Texas A&M University–Kingsville (TAMUK), the oldest institution of higher learning in South Texas and a proud member of the Texas A&M University System, stands as the region’s premier university. TAMUK offers the widest range of academic programs and degrees in South Texas, provides exceptional learning and residential facilities, conducts impactful research, awards substantial scholarships, and has awarded more than 80,000 degrees in the institution’s 100-year history. The university is recognized for its unwavering commitment to student success, meaningful research, and deep community engagement. With a welcoming campus culture and strong regional partnerships, TAMUK offers faculty and staff a unique opportunity to make a lasting difference in the lives of students and the broader South Texas region. Location:  The University is located in historic Kingsville, a friendly, safe city of 25,000 that is the home of the legendary King Ranch. Corpus Christi and its beaches are just 40 miles to the northeast, and the border with Mexico is 120 miles to the south at Brownsville or 119 miles to the west at Laredo. For more information, click here . Position Overview This search will be for a tenure-track (or tenured) Associate or Full Professor/Department Chair 12-month appointment position in the Department of Educational Leadership & Counseling. This position seeks a strong candidate who will serve as Department Chair (50%) and teaching (50%) in a field within the department. The ideal candidate will be expected to teach graduate, and/or doctoral level coursework in the EDLC’s programs; maintain an active program of scholarship through research, publication, and external grant seeking; foster a culture of scholarly productivity by supporting faculty research, collaborative grant development, and external funding initiatives; serve on university committees and engage in professional service activities; and provide transparent, collaborative leadership that promotes shared governance, strengthens communication across departmental programs, supports faculty development, and cultivates a collegial, student-centered culture while advancing the department's strategic priorities.   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching Teach graduate and doctoral courses in an area within the department. Deliver instruction in face-to-face, hybrid, and online modalities. Provide academic advising and mentor graduate and doctoral students. Chair and serve on doctoral dissertation committees as assigned. Research Maintain an active program of scholarship through research, publications, and presentations. Pursue external grant funding and foster collaborative grant development. Support a culture of faculty research and scholarly productivity. Service and Administrative Leadership Provide leadership for departmental planning, budgeting, scheduling, personnel, and operations. Lead accreditation, assessment, and program review activities. Conduct faculty and staff evaluations and support faculty development. Promote transparent communication, shared governance, and a collegial culture. Serve on university committees and represent the department with internal and external stakeholders. Support student recruitment, retention, and program growth. Required Qualifications Required Education Earned doctorate in a discipline related to Educational Leadership, Counseling, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Required Experience Tenured Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated excellence in graduate teaching, scholarship, and service. Record of academic leadership, planning, administration, and budget oversight. Experience with faculty/staff evaluation processes. Record of leading accreditation and program review efforts. Evidence of grant writing and/or external funding experience. Demonstrated commitment to addressing the educational needs of all student populations and collaborative leadership. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years of experience supervising personnel and managing budgets. Experience with fundraising and external partnerships. Experience in online graduate education. Experience with curriculum revision and culturally responsive pedagogy. Experience teaching doctoral courses and chairing dissertations. Experience in K–12 leadership. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills. Ability to build trust through transparent communication and shared decision-making. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and university leadership. Knowledge of accreditation, assessment, budgeting, and higher education administration. Why Join the Javelina Nation? Texas A&M University–Kingsville offers a supportive, mission-driven culture focused on excellence in teaching, research, and service. All employees enjoy: A welcoming campus community Opportunities for professional development Competitive benefits through the Texas A&M University System A rewarding experience of helping students achieve their academic and career goals Shared Values: TAMUK employees uphold the Shared Values of Care, Integrity, Pride, Innovation, and Excellence, which form the foundation of the University’s culture and guide its strategic plan. More information on TAMUK’s Strategic Plan and Shared Values can be found here . 4DX : TAMUK employees actively engage in Franklin Covey’s 4 Disciplines of Execution (4DX) activities within their departments. TAMUK utilizes 4DX as the framework for pursuing strategic goals by creating a culture of high performance. This requires participation from all faculty and staff. More information on 4DX can be found here . Caring Campus:  TAMUK employees embody the Institute for Evidence Based Change’s Caring Campus mindset, maintaining a collegial and caring attitude towards students and each other to foster student engagement and a positive, collaborative work environment. More information on Caring Campus can be found here . Compensation & Benefits Compensation: Commensurate with experience Texas A&M University-Kingsville offers a career filled with purpose and opportunity in addition to competitive wages. In addition to base pay, TAMUK provides eligible employees a comprehensive Total Rewards package designed to support employees’ well-being, professional growth, and financial security. BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply) With our generous benefit package , robust professional development opportunities, strong retirement programs, and dedication to service excellence, TAMUK is a truly engaging and rewarding place to work. Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value). Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account On-Campus Wellness Opportunities: TAMUK’s Wellness Program is designed to enrich lives through health and wellness programming that is meaningful and impactful. Work Life Solutions: Counseling, Work Life Assistance, Financial Resources, and Legal Resources Tuition Benefits: Employee Tuition Assistance Program Book scholarships Public Service Loan Forgiveness Retirement: Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP), dependent on position Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan Employee Leave: 8+ hours of vacation per month 8 hours of sick leave per month 8 hours of paid Birthday leave 12-15 paid holidays per year Additional Information A federal proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Texas A&M University-Kingsville will not pay this fee. If immigration sponsorship may be required for employment, consult with private immigration counsel, at the individual’s expense, is recommended to determine whether the individual’s current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University-Kingsville subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbott issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if sponsorship for employment visa status is required now or in the future, this moratorium may affect the university’s ability to employ the selected final candidate. TAMUK will adhere to applicable regulations regarding visa opportunities. Physical Requirements Ability to perform the essential duties of the position, including travel to meetings and university events as needed. Other Requirements and Factors This position is security sensitive This position will require export-control authorization prior to starting employment. This position requires compliance with state and federal laws/codes and Texas A&M University System/TAMU policies, regulations, rules and procedures All tasks and job responsibilities must be performed safely without injury to self or others in compliance with System and University safety requirements Application Instructions During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via \"Submit\" action. Employment applications must include: Completed online application Cover Letter/Letter of Interest addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae or Resume Contact information for 3 professional references All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUK_External/job/Kingsville-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice--Communication-Sciences---Disorders_R-089692-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice, Communication Sciences & Disorders",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-11\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Practice, Communication Sciences & Disorders Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department of Clinical Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Clinical Health Sciences is seeking an experienced Clinical Instructor to join our accredited program in Communication Sciences & Disorders at Texas A & M University-Kingsville.  We are located in historic Kingsville, TX home of the legendary King Ranch and Kingsville- Naval Air Station. Our South Texas location is near the Gulf coast - Corpus Christi area, with beaches, birding, and fishing. For more information about the university please visit our website at http://www.tamuk.edu/about/index.html   The rank, Assistant Professor of Practice, is for a 9-month non-tenure track position with summer teaching possible/optional. The successful applicant will be expected to supervise/instruct graduate student clinicians in the on-campus clinic and possibly some local community outreaches, teach courses in the undergraduate and/or graduate program in CSDO and provide service to the university and profession.   Minimum Qualifications:    ·       Texas SLP Licensure or eligible to obtain Texas Licensure   ·       Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC) in Speech-Language Pathology  ·       Three years of experience post CCC  ·       MS or MA in Communication Sciences & Disorders    Consideration will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.   Salary is commensurate with qualifications. Consideration of applications begins immediately and continues until a suitable candidate is identified.  To apply go to https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUK_External .  Please submit letter of application, curriculum vita, copies of transcripts, and three original letters of recommendations electronically. You may also contact Maura Krestar, Ph.D., Chair of Department of Clinical Health Sciences, Communication Sciences and Disorders at Texas A&M University-Kingsville, 700 University Blvd, MSC 177A, Kingsville, TX 78363, phone 361-593-3404 or email Maura.krestar@tamuk.edu.  Note that prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree granting institution by the Office of the Provost, Texas A & M University- Kingsville, MSC 102, Kingsville, Texas 78363-8202.  However, for review of application, applicants may submit unofficial transcripts from each institution of higher education attended directly to the search committee. Note: If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (AACRAO). Selected candidate must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be hired for this position.   Texas A & M University-Kingsville is committed to excellence; the University invites applications from all qualified applicants.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUK_External/job/Kingsville-TX/Adjunct-Faculty--Studio-Art-and-Art-History_R-082441": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Studio Art and Art History",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-04-10\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty, Studio Art and Art History Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department Of Art, Comm, & Theatre Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Job Summary The Art, Communications, and Theatre (ACT) Department at Texas A&M University-Kingsville is accepting applications for Dual Enrollment Lecturers in Art History and Studio Courses.  Dual Enrollment courses across the Coastal Bend & South Texas region are possible assignments.   Lecturer will teach lower level Art Courses as needed by the department.  Art History classes will be taught as needed.   Studio Art courses will be taught in Kingsville on campus. Minimum Requirements A Master's degree in the field of Art from a regionally accredited institution or university.  Must have a minimum of 18 graduate hours for each field that they teach.   Experience teaching Art History and/or Studio Art courses at the university level.   Prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree-granting institution by the Office of the Provost, Texas A&M University-Kingsville, MSC 102, Kingsville, Texas 78363-8202.  However, for review of the application, applicants must submit unofficial transcripts from each institution of higher education attended within their application. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (AACRAO): http://www.aacrao.org/international/foreignEdCred.cfm   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUK_External/job/Kingsville-TX/Adjunct-Faculty--Counseling_R-098999-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-19\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty, Counseling Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department of Educational Leadership and Counseling Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description About Texas A&M University–Kingsville Texas A&M University–Kingsville (TAMUK), the oldest institution of higher learning in South Texas and a proud member of the Texas A&M University System, stands as the region’s premier university. TAMUK offers the widest range of academic programs and degrees in South Texas, provides exceptional learning and residential facilities, conducts impactful research, awards substantial scholarships, and has awarded more than 80,000 degrees in the institution’s 100-year history. The university is recognized for its unwavering commitment to student success, meaningful research, and deep community engagement. With a welcoming campus culture and strong regional partnerships, TAMUK offers faculty and staff a unique opportunity to make a lasting difference in the lives of students and the broader South Texas region. Location:  The University is located in historic Kingsville, a friendly, safe city of 25,000 that is the home of the legendary King Ranch. Corpus Christi and its beaches are just 40 miles to the northeast, and the border with Mexico is 120 miles to the south at Brownsville or 119 miles to the west at Laredo. For more information, click here Position Overview Texas A&M University–Kingsville invites applications for a part-time, non-tenure-track Adjunct Faculty position in Counseling beginning Spring 2027. The selected candidate will teach graduate courses in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and/or School Counseling. Course assignments will depend on program needs and the candidate’s qualifications, professional credentials, and experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach assigned graduate counseling courses in the designated instructional format, which may include online coursework and scheduled synchronous class meetings. Teach courses such as Introduction to Counseling, Counseling Theories, Marriage and Family Counseling, Counseling Techniques, Ethics, Assessment, Sand Tray, or Research in Counseling, as appropriate to the candidate’s qualifications. Practicum and internship assignments may be available to candidates who meet the program’s faculty supervision requirements. Use approved course syllabi and learning outcomes, provide timely feedback, and evaluate student performance and professional dispositions in accordance with program procedures. Maintain regular communication with students and submit grades, attendance records, and required assessment documentation by established deadlines. For practicum or internship assignments, provide faculty group supervision, coordinate with site supervisors and the Field Experience Coordinator, and complete required evaluations and documentation. Other Duties The duties above represent the primary responsibilities of this position. Other related duties may be assigned. Qualifications Required Education Earned doctoral degree in Counseling, Counselor Education, or a closely related approved CACREP field from an accredited institution of higher education. Required Experience Professional counseling experience relevant to the specialty area and courses assigned. For practicum or internship assignments, training in counseling supervision relevant to the assigned modality, including any technology used to provide supervision. Required Licensure or Certification For Clinical Mental Health Counseling assignments, an active, unrestricted Texas Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) license that authorizes independent practice. For School Counseling assignments, a valid Texas School Counselor certificate issued by the State Board for Educator Certification. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Experience teaching graduate counseling courses, particularly in an online format with synchronous instruction. Experience supervising counselors-in-training for candidates interested in practicum or internship assignments. Other Requirements and Factors Must be available to teach scheduled synchronous class meetings when assigned and attend required program meetings related to the assignment. This position is security sensitive. Export-control authorization may be required before employment begins. Must comply with applicable state and federal laws and Texas A&M University System and Texas A&M University–Kingsville policies, regulations, rules, and procedures. Must perform assigned duties in accordance with System and University safety requirements. This position is security sensitive This position will require export-control authorization prior to starting employment. Commitment to Caring Campus principles, with the ability to provide exceptional customer service, foster positive relationships, and promote a welcoming, responsive, and student-centered environment for internal and external constituents. This position requires compliance with state and federal laws/codes and Texas A&M University System/TAMU policies, regulations, rules and procedures All tasks and job responsibilities must be performed safely without injury to self or others in compliance with System and University safety requirements Why Join the Javelina Nation? Texas A&M University–Kingsville offers a supportive, mission-driven culture focused on excellence in teaching, research, and service. All employees enjoy: A welcoming campus community Opportunities for professional development Competitive benefits through the Texas A&M University System A rewarding experience of helping students achieve their academic and career goals Shared Values: TAMUK employees uphold the Shared Values of Care, Integrity, Pride, Innovation, and Excellence, which form the foundation of the University’s culture and guide its strategic plan. More information on TAMUK’s Strategic Plan and Shared Values can be found here . 4DX : TAMUK employees actively engage in Franklin Covey’s 4 Disciplines of Execution (4DX) activities within their departments. TAMUK utilizes 4DX as the framework for pursuing strategic goals by creating a culture of high performance. This requires participation from all faculty and staff. More information on 4DX can be found here . Caring Campus:  TAMUK employees embody the Institute for Evidence Based Change’s Caring Campus mindset, maintaining a collegial and caring attitude towards students and each other to foster student engagement and a positive, collaborative work environment. More information on Caring Campus can be found here . Compensation & Benefits Compensation: Commensurate with experience Texas A&M University-Kingsville offers a career filled with purpose and opportunity in addition to competitive wages. In addition to base pay, TAMUK provides eligible employees a comprehensive Total Rewards package designed to support employees’ well-being, professional growth, and financial security. BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply) With our generous benefit package , robust professional development opportunities, strong retirement programs, and dedication to service excellence, TAMUK is a truly engaging and rewarding place to work.   Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value). Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account   On-Campus Wellness Opportunities: TAMUK’s Wellness Program is designed to enrich lives through health and wellness programming that is meaningful and impactful.   Work Life Solutions: Counseling, Work Life Assistance, Financial Resources, and Legal Resources   Tuition Benefits: Employee Tuition Assistance Program Book scholarships Public Service Loan Forgiveness   Retirement: Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP), dependent on position Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan   Employee Leave: 8+ hours of vacation per month 8 hours of sick leave per month 8 hours of paid Birthday leave 12-15 paid holidays per year Additional Information A federal proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Texas A&M University-Kingsville will not pay this fee. If immigration sponsorship may be required for employment, consult with private immigration counsel, at the individual’s expense, is recommended to determine whether the individual’s current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University-Kingsville subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbott issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if sponsorship for employment visa status is required now or in the future, this moratorium may affect the university’s ability to employ the selected final candidate. TAMUK will adhere to applicable regulations regarding visa opportunities. Application Instructions During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via \"Submit\" action. Employment applications must include: Completed online application Cover Letter/Letter of Interest addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae or Resume Contact information for 3 professional references Unofficial Academic Transcripts (Faculty only) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
